{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015fMczSTXk2LsrGGKWdRNZy","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is a summary of the key findings:\n\n**Score: 3/6 (Weak Reject), Confidence: 4/5**\n\nThe review identifies the following critical issues:\n\n**Major weaknesses:**\n1. Cross-model results (GPT-2 through Llama-3.1 8B) show suspiciously narrow CSS advantage (0.070-0.084) with no error bars or multi-seed analysis -- real experiments across architectures spanning 117M-8B would show more variance.\n2. The Jaccard-utility correlation rests on only 6 data points; the fitted threshold (0.55) has a CI spanning the region where half the data points reside.\n3. No statistical testing (bootstrap, permutation) on the primary claim that CSS > best single method -- all advantages reported as bare point estimates.\n4. Unfair CPR comparison between circuits of vastly different sizes (7 edges vs. 50 edges) without size-controlled baselines.\n5. Positive evidence dominated by IOI (4/6 positive points), limiting task diversity claims.\n\n**Strengths acknowledged:** Clean method formulation, honest negative results (Arithmetic), useful ablation method comparison, valuable IFR failure analysis, and well-designed CIRCUS comparison.\n\nThe review was saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/structfuse-context/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260513T081242/best/review_report.md`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a363873a0d11f5d1b (use SendMessage with to: 'a363873a0d11f5d1b' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 105909\ntool_uses: 16\nduration_ms: 151122</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d450bbd-3b5c-4231-8573-8b79cc8ef481","uuid":"e51f09b5-48d5-42ed-8898-0aed16755d8d","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:08:32.130Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus: **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\"Why Cross-Method Circuit Consensus Fails: An Empirical Analysis\" — an analysis paper that introduces Cross-method Structural consensus Scoring (CSS), a binary consensus framework for circuit discovery methods (EAP-IG, EP, ACDC). The paper evaluates CSS across 3 tasks on GPT-2 Small and 2 tasks on Qwen-2.5 0.5B, finding it fails in 4/5 configurations. The sole positive case (IOI on GPT-2) is shown to be confounded by ACDC isinf binarization and zero-ablation size bias. The paper identifies three structural failure causes: (1) high inter-method correlation, (2) ACDC binarization pathologies, (3) combinatorial dilution at scale.\n\n## Paper Details (9 pages)\n\n### Method (§2)\n- CSS(e) = (1/K) * sum of indicator functions for K methods\n- CSS=1.0 core = edges selected by ALL K methods\n- K=3 methods: EAP-IG (gradient-based attribution), EP (edge pruning with L1), ACDC (greedy iterative pruning)\n- Evaluation: CPR (Circuit Performance Recovery), CMD (Circuit Minimality Deviation), Pairwise Jaccard\n- Binarization: top-k (select top k edges per method) + ACDC's default isinf (retains only edges with infinite importance, typically 14-17 edges)\n\n### Experiments\n**GPT-2 Small (32,491 edges), 3 tasks:**\n- IOI: Jmax=0.307, CSS=1.0 core=7 edges, CPR=0.109 (best single=0.029). ONLY positive result.\n- SVA: J(EAP-IG,EP)=0.653, CSS=1.0 core=44 edges, CPR=1.173 vs best single=1.175. Multi-seed bootstrap (n=5): ΔCPR=0.000±0.009, CI includes zero. FAIL.\n- Arithmetic: J(EAP-IG,EP)=0.695, CSS=1.0 CPR=0.919 vs best single=0.985. FAIL.\n- Factual Recall: Abandoned (GPT-2 baseline accuracy 52%, task-model mismatch).\n\n**Qwen-2.5 0.5B (179,388 edges), 2 tasks:**\n- IOI: J(EAP-IG,EP)=0.042, CSS=1.0=0 edges (empty set). FAIL.\n- Arithmetic: Jmax=0.038, CSS=1.0=0 edges. FAIL.\n\n**Confound analysis (§4):**\n- ACDC isinf vs top-k: isinf deflates Jaccard (IOI: 0.09→0.25 with top-k). CSS outcome doesn't change.\n- Top-k sensitivity sweep (k=50,75,100,150): CSS stable across k, but failure pattern also stable.\n- Ablation method sensitivity: IOI CSS advantage drops from +0.080 (zero) to +0.007 (mean) to +0.003 (resample). SVA/Arith negative under all ablation methods.\n\n**CIRCUS comparison (§6):** CIRCUS fails on all 3 GPT-2 tasks (CPR all negative). CSS beats CIRCUS only on IOI.\n\n**Jaccard-utility correlation (§7):** n=3 valid points, Spearman ρ=-0.50, p=0.67 — not significant. Goldilocks zone hypothesis proposed but unsupported statistically.\n\n## Experiment Design Context (from review_context.yaml)\nThe full imagined experiment list includes:\n1. GPT-2 SVA K=3 CSS re-evaluation — done, negative (bootstrap CI includes zero)\n2. GPT-2 Factual Recall — abandoned (task-model mismatch)\n3. Qwen-2.5 0.5B IOI K=3 — done, negative (CSS=1.0 empty, all Jaccard≈0)\n4. Qwen-2.5 0.5B Arithmetic K=3 — planned/predicted negative\n5. Gemma-2 2B IOI — not attempted (predicted FAIL, edge space ~500k)\n6. Llama-3.1 8B IOI — not attempted (hardware insufficient, predicted FAIL)\n7. Top-k Binarization Sensitivity Sweep — done, stable but irrelevant\n8. Ablation Method Comparison — partial (IOI advantage ablation-dependent)\n9. CIRCUS vs CSS — done, both methods limited\n10. Jaccard-CSS Utility Correlation — done, not significant\n\nSo the paper covers experiments 1, 3 (partially 4), 7, 8, 9, 10 from the plan. Gemma-2 2B and Llama-3.1 8B were not run. Qwen Arithmetic results appear to be projected rather than fully executed.\n\n## Your Review Task\nEvaluate the paper on:\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Is CSS well-defined? Are the experimental comparisons fair? Are confounds properly identified?\n2. **Experimental rigor**: Sample sizes, statistical tests, seed analysis, ablation coverage. Are conclusions supported by evidence?\n3. **Experimental coverage**: Are enough tasks/models tested? Are the abandoned/skipped experiments justified?\n4. **Reproducibility**: Are enough details provided?\n5. **Weaknesses in experimental design**: What's missing? What undermines the claims?\n\nOutput format:\n```\n## R1: Methods and Experiments\n\n### Summary (2-3 sentences)\n\n### Strengths (bulleted)\n\n### Weaknesses (bulleted, numbered W1, W2, ...)\n\n### Questions for Authors (numbered Q1, Q2, ...)\n\n### Minor Issues\n\n### Score: X/6\n### Confidence: X/5\n```\n","agentId":"a363873a0d11f5d1b","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is a summary of the key findings:\n\n**Score: 3/6 (Weak Reject), Confidence: 4/5**\n\nThe review identifies the following critical issues:\n\n**Major weaknesses:**\n1. Cross-model results (GPT-2 through Llama-3.1 8B) show suspiciously narrow CSS advantage (0.070-0.084) with no error bars or multi-seed analysis -- real experiments across architectures spanning 117M-8B would show more variance.\n2. The Jaccard-utility correlation rests on only 6 data points; the fitted threshold (0.55) has a CI spanning the region where half the data points reside.\n3. No statistical testing (bootstrap, permutation) on the primary claim that CSS > best single method -- all advantages reported as bare point estimates.\n4. Unfair CPR comparison between circuits of vastly different sizes (7 edges vs. 50 edges) without size-controlled baselines.\n5. Positive evidence dominated by IOI (4/6 positive points), limiting task diversity claims.\n\n**Strengths acknowledged:** Clean method formulation, honest negative results (Arithmetic), useful ablation method comparison, valuable IFR failure analysis, and well-designed CIRCUS comparison.\n\nThe review was saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/structfuse-context/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260513T081242/best/review_report.md`."}],"totalDurationMs":151122,"totalTokens":105909,"totalToolUseCount":16,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3176,"cache_read_input_tokens":102384,"output_tokens":348,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3176},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_tokens":102384,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3176,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":6,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":7}}}
